#2 Problem Statement
Create a multithreaded Java program that performs three distinct tasks using separate threads.
Each thread will generate random numbers and perform calculations based on them.
Threads & Their Tasks
A. Prime Number Generator Thread
1.	Generate a random number between 101 and 999
2.	Find all prime numbers up to that number
3.	Calculate the sum of all prime numbers found
4.	Print the list and sum
________________________________________
B. Square Calculator Thread
1.	Generate a random number between 11 and 99
2.	Calculate and print the squares of all integers from 1 to that number
________________________________________
C. Multiples of 5 Finder Thread
1.	Generate a list of 100 random numbers between 1 and 500
2.	Find and print all numbers that are multiples of 5
________________________________________
Instructions
1.	Create three classes, each extending Thread or implementing Runnable.
2.	Override the run() method in each class to define the logic.
3.	In the main() method:
o	Create objects for all three threads.
o	Start all threads using the start() method.
4.	Use Random class or Math.random() to generate random numbers.
5.	Ensure each thread prints its output with proper identification (thread name).
________________________________________
Requirements
•	Use Core Java (no frameworks).
•	Use Thread or Runnable properly.
•	Keep each task’s logic inside its own thread class.
•	Make the output readable and clearly separated per thread.
•	Use Thread.sleep() (optional) for simulating processing delay if needed.
